==Galician==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|gl|es|pasear}} ({{etydate|1812|nocap=1}}). With the meaning 'to execute', attested since the Spanish Civil war (Fascist execution squads used to tell their victims that they were going to take a walk together).

===Pronunciation===
{{gl-pr|pasėar}}

===Verb===
{{gl-verb}}

# {{lb|gl|intransitive}} to [[take a walk]]
# {{lb|gl|transitive}} to [[walk]] {{q|a dog, etc.}}
# {{lb|gl|transitive|idiomatic}} to [[execute]]
#: {{ux|gl|Aquela tarde '''pasearon''' o seu avó|That evening they '''executed''' their grandfather}}

====Conjugation====
{{gl-conj}}

